     4	# P1's recipe (plan_depth_canon.md v8 §4): 2 x A6000, DDP + SyncBN, 32/GPU x 2
     5	# x accum 1 (BN 64), bf16-mixed, seed 42, 40,000 steps, checkpoint / 2,500.
     6	# The arm is P1's config (FLAC_AR_BVp1.json) plus exactly ONE delta,
     7	# training.canonicalize {enabled: true, img_w: 512}.
     8	#
     9	# MODE=SMOKE  25 steps, own W&B project + run namespace, checkpoint cadence
    10	#             10^6 (writes none); projects the 40k wall clock; writes the
    11	#             smoke-evidence JSON that FULL requires.
    12	# MODE=FULL   the registered 40,000-step run; needs a PASSING smoke evidence
    13	#             with the SAME HEAD and pin-manifest sha256 (+ the schema-2 GPU
    14	#             provenance under this launcher's literals, rC-F2).
    15	# DRY_RUN=1   every gate except the side-effecting / GPU ones (write probe,
    16	#             GPU memory, W&B identity), prints the exact argv, exits 0.
    17	# EXPECT_HEAD the full reviewed pin commit; HEAD must equal it (required).
    18	# DEPTH_CANON_HARNESS=<dir under /tmp with a .depth_canon_harness marker>:
    19	#             guard-suite mode -- the save root moves into <dir>/save, the W&B
    20	#             identity gate is skipped, the evidence is tagged harness=true and
    21	#             a production FULL never accepts it. Nothing else changes.
    22	#
    23	# Adapted from exp_17's yaw_aug_a6000_launch.sh with its r3 review's BLOCKING
    24	# findings applied (HEAD + content binding, smoke evidence bound to HEAD +
    25	# manifest, no pipefail around tr|grep -- the log is read ONCE into a variable
    26	# after the tee is drained, a non-finite scan in FULL too) plus plan §4 gates
    27	# (5) run-owned checkpoints, (6) NAS identity / write probe / free space,
    28	# (7) projection <= 120 h (v14; was 60 h), and (8) the GPU gate: >= 12 GiB free on each card (v14;
    29	# was 22.5 GiB) with compute processes on GPU 0/1 handled per GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY -- `shared`
    30	# (pinned, plan v14, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25): co-tenants DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd)
    31	# in the log and the SMOKE evidence, never refused; `idle`: refused (v10). It never kills anything.
    32	# Exit codes: 0 ok (DRY_RUN: every gate passed) | 2 a gate refused (CONFIG ERROR included) | 3 treatment
    33	#   banner missing | 4 non-finite values / the smoke verdict FAILED | 5 the checkpoint set is wrong | 6 endpoint
    34	#   or two-rank start missing | 7 a GPU-gate refusal (the memory floor, or an nvidia-smi answer that is not
    35	#   clean; occupancy only under GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=idle -- under `shared` co-tenants are disclosed, not
    36	#   refused), RESERVED: only gpu_refuse emits it -- the ONE transient class the watcher retries (rA A6e) |
    37	#   8 any OTHER exit 7, e.g. train.py's own status 7, remapped by the EXIT trap so a trainer failure is
    38	#   never retried (rB-F2 F2-1, Codex A2 HIGH 1) | anything else: train.py's own nonzero status, passed
    39	#   through (terminal).
    40	#
    41	# Write targets: the NAS save root (checkpoints, launch marker, write probe), this experiment
    42	# folder (logs, smoke evidence, checkpoint manifest) and -- the one expected extra target --
    43	# W&B's run metadata in the checkout's repo-local `wandb/` (train.py's WandbLogger is built
    44	# without a save_dir). r3b-F1 (Codex r3b review) added: the flac interpreter pin, the tie-audit
    45	# gate, the GPU-occupancy gate, finite-loss + latency smoke evidence, content-scoped binding.
    46	#
    47	# Written by the exp_25 Coder seat (Claude Opus, max effort) per plan_depth_canon.md v8 §4.
    48	# ============================================================================
