  Both `na` and `na_other` are tested at [test_depth_canon_autolaunch.py:289](/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-25-depth-canon/src/tests/test_depth_canon_autolaunch.py:289). Removing `nounits` breaks the exact-query stub and clean-poll tests; removing the numeric check breaks both J2 cases. Existing three-poll, token, rc-7 cap, literal rung, scrub, tee-drain, and idle-policy behavior remains covered.

  Projecting away the watcher-only `process_name` field, the launcher and watcher accept the same UUID/PID/used-memory grammar. The watcher additionally rejects a comma-containing process name; that is conservative and cannot cause a wrong launch.

- **R3 — RESOLVED.** The watcher is part of the clone overlay at [depth_canon_guardtests.sh:26](/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-25-depth-canon/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_guardtests.sh:26), and U15 reads both scripts through `git -C "$R" show HEAD:` at lines 612–625. U15b’s clone-only 23,040 flip proves isolation at lines 635–643.

